WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.410
Step one.

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.685
Everything in this demo lives in one GitHub repository: the app,

00:00:03.735 --> 00:00:07.931
the Kubernetes manifests, the Bicep templates, and the workflows that connect them.

00:00:07.981 --> 00:00:09.668
This is the template repository.

00:00:09.718 --> 00:00:13.793
Signed in to GitHub, select Use this template, then Create a new repository,

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:15.258
and you have your own copy.

00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:21.588
The src folder holds three small Node.js services: the membership API, the bed API,

00:00:21.638 --> 00:00:22.732
and the portal.

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:27.680
Under k8s base are the Kubernetes manifests: deployments, services, autoscalers,

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.216
disruption budgets, and network policies.

00:00:30.266 --> 00:00:33.296
The infra folder has the Bicep template and its modules.

00:00:33.346 --> 00:00:36.652
The bootstrap folder holds the one-time Azure setup, as code.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:40.991
There are seven workflows, from CI and Code QL to infrastructure, app delivery,

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.682
demo scenarios, and the publishing of this guide.

00:00:43.732 --> 00:00:48.319
Step three needs two numbers: the repository ID and the owner ID.

00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:50.174
The GitHub API shows both.

00:00:51.224 --> 00:00:55.154
The README links back to this guide and summarises what the demo covers.

00:00:55.204 --> 00:00:59.460
And this guide itself is published from the same repository, with GitHub Pages.
